Package: estheRineq
Type: Package
Title: Epidemiological Statistics Toolkit for Health Inequality Estimation and Reporting
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(
    given = "Akram",
    family = "Hernández-Vásquez",
    role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "akram.hernandez@users.noreply.github.com",
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1431-2526")
  )
Description: Unites complex-survey health econometrics and epidemiological health
    inequality surveillance and reporting. Provides rank-dependent concentration
    indices (standard, generalized, modified, Wagstaff, Erreygers, extended, and
    symmetric) with exact O(N log N) Gateaux influence-function linearization,
    stratified multistage ultimate-cluster variance, replicate weights, and
    Rao-Wu-Yue survey bootstrap inference; classical univariate inequality indices
    (Gini, S-Gini, Atkinson, generalized entropy, Palma, S80/S20) and subgroup
    decompositions; all 21 World Health Organization Health Inequality Monitor
    summary measures; modern logistic and modified-Poisson slope and relative
    indices of inequality (SII and RII); direct and indirect epidemiological rate
    standardization with Dobson and Byar confidence intervals; econometric health-need
    standardization and horizontal inequity; reference-invariant Wagstaff,
    recentered influence-function (RIF), and counterfactual RIF-Oaxaca
    decompositions; editorial visualizations (Pelotas equiplots, concentration
    curves, gradient plots, decomposition forest plots, and Spiegelhalter funnel
    plots); and multilingual (English, Spanish, Portuguese) STROBE-Equity
    exports to Markdown, LaTeX, HTML, Excel, and Word.
